Z||000000||dyno_78||03-06-2001||02:32 PM||||Hi   Hoping to get some help.  My Fiero only likes to start when cold.  After running for approx. 10 min. won't start once turned off.  Actually in the last week or so it sometimes won't even start when cold.  Seems to just start whenever it feels like it.  I'm wondering if this could possibly be the fuel pump?  <p>[This message has been edited by dyno_78 (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||03-06-2001||05:42 PM||||Sounds like an ignition module to me.  When they age they become finiky with temperature.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||03-06-2001||05:56 PM||||I second the Ignition Module.<P>Welcome to the forum<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||03-06-2001||06:03 PM||||No clue, but welcome to the forum<P>btw: my 85 se works  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||03-06-2001||06:24 PM||||I am assuming it turns over when hot.<BR>get your hands on a fuel pressure gauge if you think it is the fuel pump...<P>Easier to do is have someone try to start it hot, and chack for spark via a plug wire to the block   Not too much now as fuel will be getting dumped into the motor.  <BR>those two things will check the two fundamental components, fuel and spark.<BR>We can procede from there.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dyno_78||03-06-2001||06:39 PM||||Thanks for all your help.  Yes it is turning over when hot, just not starting, and yes there is spark.  Do you think it could have to do with the oil pressure sensor?||||reg||1
Z||000006||KRMFiero||03-07-2001||06:47 AM||||I'll try to be helpful, if something doesnt start  I always try starting fluid first, worth a shot maybe?   If it starts on that then it is aproblem in the fuel lines or something<P><BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||03-07-2001||12:00 PM||||Be really careful with starting fluid "death fluid" as known by mechanics. I use a little carb cleaner instead. Ether can destroy an engine with one big squirt. It causes overreving and has no lube properties to it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||4
